<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11260" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαιωρ-έομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hang down from, hover about,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				234
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἔνθεν καὶ ἔνθεν</span>
			<i>hang without support</i> at either end, as a fractured limb
			supported only by the bandage at the fracture, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Art.</u>
				63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				15.11.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				44.23.6
			</span></i>, Megesap. eund.<i><span class="en">
				44.24.13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ὕλης ἡ κόμη μετέωρος ἀπῃώρηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procop.
				</span></i>
			 Gaz.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ecphr.</u>
				p.158B.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be uplifted,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Astr.</u>
				19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later in 
				Act.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαιωρέω</span></b> , <i>let hang
				down,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοκάμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.55
				</span></i>
			; <i>lift up</i> a garment, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				11.6.9
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
